  "1db92073c34f3bb51e63d9a52893a7cf5ad30b1750fa9d87e17a7e61363885b6": {
    "fact_rationales": {
      "F12": "The presence of a diffuse bland spindle cell proliferation with comma-shaped nuclei and a collagenous matrix in the superficial wall is more typical of neurofibromatosis-related tumors, such as Malignant Peripheral Nerve Sheath Tumor (B4.1) and Neurofibrosarcoma (B4.5).",
      "F13": "The dense, perivascular spindle cell proliferation with prominent cytological atypia, frequent mitoses, and an infiltrative growth pattern in the deeper wall is highly suggestive of a malignant tumor, particularly Malignant Peripheral Nerve Sheath Tumor (B4.1) and Neurofibrosarcoma (B4.5).",
      "F14": "The tumor's close contact with peripheral nerves is a characteristic feature of nerve sheath tumors, making Malignant Peripheral Nerve Sheath Tumor (B4.1) and Neurofibrosarcoma (B4.5) more likely.",
      "F15": "The immunohistochemical profile, with positivity for S100, p16, neurofilaments, and CD56, and negativity for other markers, is highly specific for Malignant Peripheral Nerve Sheath Tumor (B4.1) and Neurofibrosarcoma (B4.5), which are known to express these markers."
    },
